### Description
This Terraform program creates an Elastic Beanstalk application with an application version lifecycle. The application version will be retained for 5 days in an S3 bucket. The program includes the necessary IAM roles and policies to allow Elastic Beanstalk to manage resources.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "elastic_beanstalk_service_role" {
  name = "elastic-beanstalk-service-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticbeanstalk.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_elastic_beanstalk_service_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkWebTier"
  role       = aws_iam_role.elastic_beanstalk_service_role.name
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "my_application" {
  name = "my-application"

  appversion_lifecycle {
    service_role = aws_iam_role.elastic_beanstalk_service_role.arn
    max_age_in_days = 5
    delete_source_from_s3 = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "application_versions_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-application-versions-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration" "application_versions_lifecycle" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.application_versions_bucket.id

  rule {
    id     = "expire-old-versions"
    status = "Enabled"

    expiration {
      days = 5
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version" "my_application_version" {
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  bucket      = aws_s3_bucket.application_versions_bucket.bucket
  key         = "my-application-version.zip"
  name        = "v1"
}

resource "random_string" "suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role and Policy Attachment**: An IAM role named `elastic-beanstalk-service-role` is created with an assume role policy that allows Elastic Beanstalk to assume the role. The AWS managed policy `AWSElasticBeanstalkWebTier` is attached to this role.
3. **Elastic Beanstalk Application**: An Elastic Beanstalk application named `my-application` is created. The application version lifecycle is configured to retain versions for 5 days and delete the source from S3.
4. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket named `my-application-versions-bucket-{random_suffix}` is created to store application versions. Versioning is enabled on the bucket.
5. **S3 Bucket Lifecycle Configuration**: A lifecycle rule is added to the S3 bucket to expire objects after 5 days.
6. **Elastic Beanstalk Application Version**: An application version named `v1` is created and uploaded to the S3 bucket.

This configuration ensures that the Elastic Beanstalk application and its versions are properly set up with the required IAM roles and policies, and the application versions are retained for 5 days in an S3 bucket.

