### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Lex bot using the `aws_lex_bot` resource. The bot is configured with basic settings such as name, locale, and child-directed status. It also includes an abort statement and a clarification prompt. The program ensures that all required attributes are specified and uses default values where necessary.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lex_bot" "lex_bot" {
  name                = "MyLexBot"
  locale              = "en-US"
  child_directed      = false
  create_version      = true
  description         = "A sample Lex bot created using Terraform"
  detect_sentiment    = true
  enable_model_improvements = true
  idle_session_ttl_in_seconds = 300
  nlu_intent_confidence_threshold = 0.7
  process_behavior    = "BUILD"
  voice_id            = "Joanna"

  abort_statement {
    message {
      content_type = "PlainText"
      content      = "Sorry, I didn't understand that. Can you please try again?"
    }
  }

  clarification_prompt {
    max_attempts = 2
    message {
      content_type = "PlainText"
      content      = "I'm sorry, I didn't understand that. Can you please repeat?"
    }
  }

  intent {
    intent_name   = "GreetingIntent"
    intent_version = "$LATEST"
  }

  timeouts {
    create = "10m"
    update = "10m"
    delete = "10m"
  }
}
```

