### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Kendra data source with specified URL exclusion and inclusion patterns. The program includes the necessary configuration for the Kendra data source, including the index ID, name, type, and the configuration block where URL patterns can be defined.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  index_id = "example-index-id"
  name     = "example-kendra-datasource"
  type     = "WEBCRAWLER"

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      urls {
        seed_url_configuration {
          seed_urls = ["https://example.com"]
        }
        url_inclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/included/*"]
        url_exclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/excluded/*"]
      }
    }
  }

  role_arn = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/kendra-crawler-role"
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **Kendra Data Source Resource**: 
  - `index_id`: A placeholder value for the Kendra index ID. Replace `"example-index-id"` with the actual index ID.
  - `name`: The name of the Kendra data source.
  - `type`: The type of data source, set to `WEBCRAWLER`.
  - `configuration`: The configuration block for the web crawler, including:
    - `seed_url_configuration`: The seed URLs to start crawling from.
    - `url_inclusion_patterns`: Patterns to include in the crawl.
    - `url_exclusion_patterns`: Patterns to exclude from the crawl.
  - `role_arn`: The ARN of the IAM role that Kendra assumes to access the data source. Replace `"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/kendra-crawler-role"` with the actual ARN of your IAM role.

