### Description
This Terraform program creates a custom DAX (DynamoDB Accelerator) parameter group. The parameter group is configured with specific parameters to optimize the performance of DAX clusters. The program includes the necessary AWS provider configuration and ensures that the DAX service is enabled in the specified region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "custom_dax_parameter_group" {
  name        = "custom-dax-parameter-group"
  description = "Custom parameter group for DAX"

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_read_throughput_limit"
    value = "100"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_write_throughput_limit"
    value = "50"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_record_ttl"
    value = "3600"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to any other valid AWS region where DAX is supported.
- **DAX Parameter Group**: A custom DAX parameter group named `custom-dax-parameter-group` is created. It includes three parameters:
  - `dax_read_throughput_limit`: Sets the maximum read throughput limit for the DAX cluster.
  - `dax_write_throughput_limit`: Sets the maximum write throughput limit for the DAX cluster.
  - `dax_record_ttl`: Sets the time-to-live (TTL) for records in the DAX cluster.

This configuration ensures that the DAX parameter group is properly set up with the specified parameters, optimizing the performance of your DAX clusters.

