### Description
This Terraform program creates a managed Amazon Managed Streaming for Kafka (MSK) cluster in the `us-east-1` region and configures it to log to an Amazon Kinesis Firehose delivery stream. The program includes the necessary IAM roles and policies to allow the MSK cluster to send logs to the Kinesis Firehose delivery stream.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "msk_cluster_logs_firehose" {
  name        = "msk-cluster-logs-firehose"
  destination = "extended_s3"

  extended_s3_configuration {
    role_arn   = aws_iam_role.msk_cluster_logging_role.arn
    bucket_arn = "arn:aws:s3:::msk-logs-bucket"
    prefix     = "msk-logs/"
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "msk_cluster_logging_role" {
  name = "msk-cluster-logging-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "msk_cluster_logging_policy" {
  name = "msk-cluster-logging-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.msk_cluster_logging_role.name

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "firehose:PutRecord",
          "firehose:PutRecordBatch"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.msk_cluster_logs_firehose.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_msk_cluster" "managed_msk_cluster" {
  cluster_name           = "managed-msk-cluster"
  kafka_version          = "2.8.1"
  number_of_broker_nodes = 3

  broker_node_group_info {
    client_subnets = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0123456789abcdef1", "subnet-0123456789abcdef2"]
    instance_type  = "t3.medium"
    security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]
  }

  logging_info {
    broker_logs {
      cloudwatch_logs {
        enabled   = false
      }
      firehose {
        delivery_stream = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.msk_cluster_logs_firehose.name
        enabled         = true
      }
      s3 {
        enabled = false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: A Kinesis Firehose delivery stream named `msk-cluster-logs-firehose` is created with an extended S3 configuration. The delivery stream sends logs to an S3 bucket named `msk-logs-bucket`.
3. **IAM Role for MSK Logging**: An IAM role named `msk-cluster-logging-role` is created with a trust policy that allows Firehose to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy**: An IAM role policy named `msk-cluster-logging-policy` is attached to the IAM role, granting it permissions to put records into the Kinesis Firehose delivery stream.
5. **Managed MSK Cluster**: A managed MSK cluster named `managed-msk-cluster` is created with three broker nodes. The cluster is configured to log to the Kinesis Firehose delivery stream using the IAM role created earlier.

