### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) parameter group. The parameter group is configured with a specific set of parameters to optimize the performance and behavior of DAX clusters.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "dax_parameter_group" {
  name        = "my-dax-parameter-group"
  description = "Parameter group for DAX cluster"

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_read_throughput_limit"
    value = "100"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_write_throughput_limit"
    value = "50"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_record_ttl"
    value = "3600"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up a DAX parameter group named `my-dax-parameter-group` with three parameters: `dax_read_throughput_limit`, `dax_write_throughput_limit`, and `dax_record_ttl`. These parameters help control the throughput limits and record time-to-live settings for the DAX cluster. The provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.

