### Description
This Terraform program creates two S3 buckets: one for storing data (`main_bucket`) and another for storing access logs (`log_bucket`). The `main_bucket` is configured to log its access logs to the `log_bucket`.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "main_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-main-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "log_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-log-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "log-delivery-write"

  logging {
    target_bucket = aws_s3_bucket.log_bucket.bucket
    target_prefix = "log/"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_logging" "main_bucket_logging" {
  bucket        = aws_s3_bucket.main_bucket.bucket
  target_bucket = aws_s3_bucket.log_bucket.bucket
  target_prefix = "logs/"

  target_grant {
    permission = "READ_ACP"
    grantee {
      type = "Group"
      uri  = "http://acs.amazonaws.com/groups/s3/LogDelivery"
    }
  }

  target_grant {
    permission = "WRITE"
    grantee {
      type = "Group"
      uri  = "http://acs.amazonaws.com/groups/s3/LogDelivery"
    }
  }
}

resource "random_string" "suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Main Bucket (`main_bucket`)**: This S3 bucket is created with a unique name using a random string suffix. It is set to private ACL and has versioning enabled.
3. **Log Bucket (`log_bucket`)**: This S3 bucket is created with a unique name using a random string suffix. It is set to `log-delivery-write` ACL to allow the S3 service to write logs to this bucket. The logging configuration is set up to store logs in the same bucket under the `log/` prefix.
4. **Logging Configuration (`main_bucket_logging`)**: This resource configures the `main_bucket` to log its access logs to the `log_bucket`. The `target_grant` blocks ensure that the S3 Log Delivery group has the necessary permissions to write logs to the `log_bucket`.
5. **Random String (`suffix`)**: A random string resource is used to append a unique suffix to the bucket names to ensure uniqueness across different deployments.

