### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Elastic File System (EFS) and attaches a lifecycle policy to it. The EFS file system is configured with basic settings, and the lifecycle policy specifies transitions for data storage classes.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "efs_file_system" {
  creation_token = "my-unique-token"  # Unique identifier for the EFS file system
  performance_mode = "generalPurpose"  # Performance mode for the EFS file system
  throughput_mode = "bursting"  # Throughput mode for the EFS file system

  lifecycle_policy {
    transition_to_archive = "AFTER_30_DAYS"  # Transition data to archive after 30 days
    transition_to_ia      = "AFTER_60_DAYS"  # Transition data to IA after 60 days
  }
}

# Note: aws_efs_lifecycle_policy is not a valid resource type in the AWS provider schema.
# The lifecycle policy is defined directly within the aws_efs_file_system resource.
```

This Terraform configuration sets up an EFS file system with a specified performance and throughput mode. The lifecycle policy is embedded within the EFS file system resource, specifying transitions for data storage classes. The provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region, but you can change this to any other valid AWS region.

